      "pins": ["REG3.1", "FCC2.11", "FCC2.27", "FCC2.50", "FCC2.75", "FCC2.100", "FCC2.21", "NAVC2.19", "NAVC2.32", "NAVC2.48", "NAVC2.64", "NAVC2.13"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V", "+3V3", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad11)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad27)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad50)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad75)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad100)", "unconnected-(FCC2-VDDA-Pad21)", "unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad19)", "unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad32)", "unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad48)", "unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad64)", "VDDA_NAVC"],
      "observed": "The regulator output REG3.1 is on +3.3V, while +3V3 is a separate net. The FCC and NAVC VDD pins are listed as unconnected; FCC VDDA is also unconnected, and NAVC VDDA is on an isolated VDDA_NAVC net.",
      "expected": "The specification says the 3.3 V rail feeds both MCUs. The regulator output should therefore reach the MCUs’ VDD pins, with their analog supply pins connected as required by the MCU datasheets.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3.3V\") ... (node (ref \"REG3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"OUT\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"216\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad11)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"276\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad19)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"163\") (name \"VDDA_NAVC\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"VDDA\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3 V feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU supply pins are not connected to the regulator rail, so the FCC and NAVC may fail to power up or operate. The separated 3.3 V nets also leave the intended rail distribution incomplete.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["FCC2", "UART3_FCC2"],
      "pins": ["FCC2.48", "FCC2.73", "UART3_FCC2.3", "UART3_FCC2.4"],
      "nets": ["NET0037", "NET0151"],
      "observed": "Both STM32H753 VCAP pins are connected directly to pins on the UART3_FCC2 connector: FCC2.48 shares NET0037 with UART3_FCC2.3, and FCC2.73 shares NET0151 with UART3_FCC2.4.",
      "expected": "VCAP pins are for the MCU’s internal regulator and should have the datasheet-required capacitors, not be routed to external UART connector pins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"28\") (name \"NET0037\") (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC2\") (pin \"3\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"97\") (name \"NET0151\") (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC2\") (pin \"4\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU’s internal core supply may be unstable or fail to operate, and connecting those nodes to external equipment can further load or disturb the VCAP pins.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present: the MCU supply pins are disconnected from the regulator’s 3.3 V output, and both FCC VCAP pins are routed to UART connector pins. Either issue can prevent reliable MCU operation."
}

